  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "5d8a892952d1005f7918d544bbab287fa2d02d11",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2618257316,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Help??\n\nI thought this was going to be straightforward, but I am getting the linking errors locally as well.  I've tried several tricks to try to pull either the global variable (or a getter wrapper to it) including referencing them within epan.c with no success.  Don't understand why wireshark.lib isn't pulling in the data from dot11decrypt.obj.  Is $\\<TARGET_OBJECTS:crypt\\> not the right approach?  (seems to work otherwise)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-07-10T16:55:20.548Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-07-10T16:55:20.548Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 398004364,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
